# kitchen_sink C++ bindings

A header-only C++17 wrapper over the `kitchen_sink` C ABI. `kitchen_sink.hpp`
includes the C header beside it; every declaration lives in
`namespace kitchen_sink`.

## Prerequisites

- CMake 3.14 or later
- A C++17 compiler
- The `kitchen_sink` native library (`libkitchen_sink.so`, `libkitchen_sink.dylib`, or
  `kitchen_sink.dll`)

## Use with CMake

```cmake
add_subdirectory(path/to/cpp)
add_executable(app main.cpp)
target_link_libraries(app PRIVATE kitchen_sink::cpp)
```

`kitchen_sink::cpp` adds this directory to the include path, requires
C++17, and links the native library: the file named by the `KITCHEN_SINK_LIBRARY`
CMake cache variable or environment variable when set, or else
`kitchen_sink` by name.

```cpp
#include "kitchen_sink.hpp"
```

The first free function, constructor, or static member you call checks
that the linked library matches these headers and throws
`kitchen_sink::LoadError` if it doesn't; call `kitchen_sink::check_library()`
at startup to check eagerly.

